# Source manifest — reproducible-by-reference (Invariant 3).
# Matt Pocock's agent skills (MIT). Ingested 2026-08-02 so the corpus can answer questions about wayfinder/grilling/research/to-spec and the design rationale behind them (.changeset/, .out-of-scope/, docs/) rather than relying on a session's summary of a SKILL.md.
# ⚠️ `ref` is the RELEASE branch, not `main`, and that is deliberate.
# `kb-manifest-add` wrote `ref = main` while pinning f34d927 — a commit that is
# NOT an ancestor of main (`git merge-base --is-ancestor` -> false; main is
# 2ab9580, this commit's parent). f34d927 lives only on
# origin/changeset-release/main, the changesets bot's release branch, and it is
# the commit whose CHANGELOG.md carries the consumed changeset rationale that
# sources/extractions/mattpocock-skills-docs.json was extracted from.
#
# Correcting `ref` rather than re-pinning to main keeps the manifest TRUTHFUL
# about what was actually extracted; re-pinning to 2ab9580 would leave the
# CHANGELOG chunk describing bytes absent from the pin. The cost is that a
# release branch can be force-updated, which would surface as
# `reference is not a tree` — a REAL defect signature, not a transient
# (persistence-gate-retry.md), so it fails loudly rather than silently.
url = https://github.com/mattpocock/skills
ref = changeset-release/main
commit = f34d927194a521688da962fff50708f6238d06af
kind = docs
